== street | WEEKEND · SHOPPING STREET | busy European shopping street with shop windows and shopping bags | walkin
zara (cheer): Quddus! My first stipend arrived! I bought boots, a coat, three bags, and a lamp shaped like a cat.
quddus (wave): Nice lamp. Have you paid your rent?
zara (shock): Rent... is this month?
quddus (facepalm): Every month, Zara. Let's make a budget before the cat lamp eats your stipend.

== living | THAT NIGHT · STUDENT ROOM | small student room at night with a desk, a cat-shaped lamp and a calculator | sofa
quddus (talk): Pay the fixed things first: rent, phone, transport pass. Then food. Then fun.
> 1f4b0 | SIMPLE BUDGET | 1f3e0 Rent + bills first | 1f354 Food + transport | 1f4b8 Fun money, with a limit | 1f4c8 Savings, even a little
zara (think): How do I stop overspending?
quddus (point): Write down everything you spend for one month. Cook more, buy second-hand, and use student discounts.
zara (worried): And if there's an emergency?
quddus (thumbs): That's why you save a little every month. Even small savings become a safety net.
zara (cheer): Budget done. Cat lamp stays. Fourth bag goes back to the shop!
